<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Sorokin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Sorokin was a Kuban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> officer and Red commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>. In 1918 he commanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a> against Denikin's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a>. In October 1918 he had leaders of the North Caucasian Soviet Republic arrested and shot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyatigorsk">Pyatigorsk</a> and was declared an outlaw; captured at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stavropol">Stavropol</a>, he was killed in prison on 1 November 1918.</p></div>
